comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T15:27:27.544Z","harness:codex","Implementation boundary confirmed: token-budget gate environment must explicitly disable telemetry so health/output verdicts do not depend on ambient queue/network state; representative-gate changes will follow shared runtime enforcement."
  "2026-08-13T17:12:52.045Z","harness:codex","Evidence for telemetry-independence tranche: token-budget measurement explicitly disables telemetry, persists a 32-surface format-aware ratchet, and includes a same-run 10,465-token negative control that must exceed the 6,000-token JSON default. Focused gate tests and exact 7,262-test coverage passed. Isolated import-cost and CLI-transport performance gates passed with ratchets unchanged; loaded composite runs showed transient host-load overruns, so no threshold was weakened. This item remains open because per-gate hosted/local equivalence and a declared health warning-collection bound remain to be completed."
